# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Qeda — environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in whichever providers you want to
# use. `.env.local` is gitignored; never commit real credentials.
#
# These files are loaded into process.env by src/main/env.ts when the app
# starts (electron-vite only forwards VITE_*-prefixed vars, and these keys are
# deliberately unprefixed). Real environment variables always win over the
# file. In a packaged build the `.env*` files are not shipped, so set keys in
# the app's Settings dialog instead.
#
# All providers below speak the OpenAI chat-completions protocol and are wired
# up through @ai-sdk/openai-compatible. At startup the app picks the first
# provider below that has a key AND a curated free model, so setting just
# GROQ_API_KEY is enough to start on a free tier.
#
# You can also set keys in the app's Settings dialog instead; those are
# encrypted with Electron safeStorage and take priority over the environment.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Free / free-tier coding providers (checked in this order) ───────────────

# Groq — very fast open-weight inference. Free tier is rate limited.
# Free models: openai/gpt-oss-120b, openai/gpt-oss-20b
GROQ_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — one key, hundreds of models. Models ending in `:free` cost
# nothing (~20 req/min, 200 req/day).
# Free models: qwen/qwen3.8-27b:free, z-ai/glm-5.2:free, …
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini — Flash models are on the free tier.
# Free models: gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-3.1-flash-lite, gemini-2.5-flash
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# NVIDIA NIM — hosted open-weight models with free credits, low rate limit.
# Free models: moonshotai/kimi-k2.6, z-ai/glm-5.2, openai/gpt-oss-120b
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=

# Cohere — trial keys are free but rate limited and not for production.
# Model ids change often, so the app loads them live from /models.
COHERE_API_KEY=

# OpenCode Zen — one key for curated coding models (GPT-5.x, Claude, Gemini,
# Grok, Kimi, …) served through https://opencode.ai/zen/v1.
#
# NOTE: Zen's `-free` models are rejected with HTTP 403 FreeTierError when the
# call does not come from the OpenCode client itself, so this provider is NOT
# eligible for automatic selection and has no curated free models. Add credits
# to the Zen account and pick a paid model from the live list in Settings.
OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY=

# ─── Multi-provider gateway / paid providers ────────────────────────────────

# Vercel AI Gateway — one key for many providers (billed per token)
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─── Local models ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ollama needs no key, only a running server. Free and fully offline.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# ─── External services ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Each powers a specific capability and can also be set in the app's
# Settings dialog (encrypted with OS-level storage), which takes priority over
# the environment. Providing any *one* search key is enough for advancedSearch
# to work — the agent picks the first configured provider.

# Web search
TAVILY_API_KEY=
EXA_API_KEY=
# Optional second Exa key, used when the first is rate limited.
EXA_API_KEY_2=
SERPER_API_KEY=

# Scraping (renders JavaScript-heavy pages to markdown)
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# Documentation lookup (version-specific library docs + code snippets)
CONTEXT7_API_KEY=

# Images (stock photography for notebooks). Search only needs the access key.
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=
UNSPLASH_SECRET_KEY=

# Speech
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
CARTESIA_API_KEY=

# ─── RAG / embeddings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional, and separate from the chat provider on purpose: most free chat
# tiers (Groq, OpenRouter :free) serve no embeddings endpoint at all.
#
# Leave BOTH of these EMPTY and the app picks for itself: the first curated
# model in src/main/ai/embedding-config.ts whose provider you have keyed. With
# a GEMINI_API_KEY set that is the line below, and it needs no other change.
#
#   EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=gemini  EMBEDDING_MODEL=gemini-embedding-001
#
# gemini-embedding-001 emits 3072 dimensions by default but exactly 1536 when
# the app asks for that width, so it matches the default index below. Verified
# against the live endpoint.
#
# Verified dead, do not use:
#   nvidia/llama-3.2-nv-embedqa-1b-v2 -> HTTP 410, end of life 2026-05-18
#   text-embedding-004                 -> HTTP 404 on the OpenAI-compat route
# Live NVIDIA alternatives (widths vary, and are checked on first use):
#   nvidia/llama-3.2-nv-embedqa-1b-v1, nvidia/nv-embedqa-mistral-7b-v2,
#   snowflake/arctic-embed-l
#
# EMBEDDING_DIM is fixed the first time the database is opened: the sqlite-vec
# `vec0` table is created at that width and cannot be resized. A model whose
# vectors do not match is refused with both numbers rather than written, so a
# mismatch can never corrupt the index. Changing it means deleting vellum.db and
# re-running the index tools.
EMBEDDING_DIM=1536
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=
EMBEDDING_MODEL=

# ─── Application ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development
# Renderer dev-server port for `npm start`
PORT=1212

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Held by .env.local but NOT read by the app yet
#
# These credentials exist in this project's `.env.local`, but no module under
# src/main reads them: the listed capability has no implementation. They are
# documented here so the template describes the environment truthfully, and so
# the next person does not re-discover them. Nothing below has an effect until
# a client + tool is written for it.
#
#   DAYTONA_*      sandboxed cloud compute (create sandbox, exec commands)
#   E2B_API_KEY    second sandbox provider (Linux microVMs)
#   QDRANT_*       hosted vector database (app RAG is local sqlite-vec today)
#   COMPOSIO_*     third-party tool/integration catalogue (Gmail, Slack, …)
#   KERNEL_*       cloud browser automation
#   JULES_*        async cloud coding agent (Google)
#   VERCEL_*       deployments + Vercel Sandbox
#   V0_*           UI generation
#   APPWRITE_*     hosted backend (auth/db/storage)
#   R2_*           S3-compatible object storage
#   TRIGGER_*      background job orchestration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# DAYTONA_API_KEY=
# DAYTONA_API_URL=https://app.daytona.io/api
# E2B_API_KEY=
# QDRANT_URL=
# QDRANT_API_KEY=
# COMPOSIO_API_KEY=
# KERNEL_API_KEY=
# JULES_API_KEY=
# VERCEL_TOKEN=
# V0_API_KEY=
# APPWRITE_API_KEY=
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# TRIGGER_SECRET_KEY=
